# WorkspaceHost seam: LocalWorkspaceHost behind every route that touches a workspace

## What to build

A behaviour-preserving refactor of `apps/graph-manager` (nothing under `packages/graph-execution/src` may change in this task). Create the `WorkspaceHost` interface (`src/server/host/types.ts`) and its open-source implementation `LocalWorkspaceHost` (`src/server/host/local.ts`), which does exactly what the code does today: PTY spawns (`terminals.ts`), engine starts (`routes/runs.ts`, `routes/resume.ts`), file reads (`routes/specs.ts`, `routes/inspect.ts`), run listing and detail (`runs.ts`), and the git calls of Create PR (`pr.ts`, `specdone.ts`). Add the new operations the sessions work needs (`prepare` = clone or reuse + check out a branch, `changes`, `save`, `discard`, `pushBranch`, `activity`, `loginFiles`, `stat`). Routes get a host only through the new `AppContext.hostFor(workspaceId, user)` (this task: always the one shared `LocalWorkspaceHost`; a later sessions task makes it session-aware). A shared vitest contract suite `src/server/host/contract.ts` (`hostContractSuite`) runs against `LocalWorkspaceHost` with a temp bare git remote; a later task runs the same suite against a remote agent, so the suite must only use the public `WorkspaceHost` API plus the plain files of the bare remote. Every existing test must keep passing unchanged (except call-site signature updates in tests that call the refactored helpers directly).

The db-store task (dependency, already merged) created `src/server/identity.ts` (`export interface User { id: string; name: string; email?: string }`, `ADMIN_USER`, `req.user`), `src/server/store.ts` (`Store.forUser(user) → UserStore { get(); update(fn); reviewers() }`, `AppContext.store: Store`) and `src/server/db/`. Read `app.ts`, `store.ts` and one route first to see how routes now get the per-user store (`const us = await ctx.store.forUser(req.user)`), and keep that pattern wherever this task touches store reads. Task 1 changed these signatures (use them as they are now in the code): `resolveRunHome(workspacesDir, us, id)`, `connFor`/`clientFor(ctx, us, kind)`, `liveRunIn(ctx, us, home)`, `prStatus`/`startPr`/`projectPrStatus`/`startProjectPr(..., us, ...)` take the caller's `UserStore`; `projectsOf(data)` / `projectOf(data, id)` in store.ts replace `store.projects()` / `store.project()`; `AppContext.db: Db` exists; test helpers `memoryDb()`, `testStore()` and `appWithLogin` (in-memory SQLite) are in test-helpers.ts. Where this task changes a function's parameters, keep the `us` parameter and add `host` next to it (e.g. `prStatus(ctx, us, host, ws, runId)`).

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts` (lines 39–102, 106–123) — `AppContext`, how `TerminalManager`, `ViewCache`, `Sandboxes` are built; the error handler that must learn `HostError`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/terminals.ts` (lines 27–43 `CreateTerminal`, 53–65 options, 73–95 `Term`, 102–104 `STRIPPED_ENV`, 132–156 `terminalEnv`, 222–329 `TerminalManager.create/spawn/wire/restart`, 437–444 `processOf`) — the PTY code that moves behind `spawnPty`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/terminals.ts` (lines 40–120) — `POST /api/terminals`, restart.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/runs.ts` (lines 47–55 `insideWorkspace`, 57–60 `engineCommand`, 76–100 `engineEnv`/`startEngine`, 102–120 listing/detail, 122–228 start) — engine start and run listing.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/resume.ts` (lines 20–29, 35–125) — resume reads `state.json`/`suite.json`, the lock, and starts the engine.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/specs.ts` (whole file, 132 lines) — spec list (mtime, size, title, symlinks skipped) and spec file read (1 MiB cap, symlink refused).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/inspect.ts` (whole file) — branch/changes/tasksDir/spec inspection.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/runs.ts` (lines 257–298 `summarize`, 286–291 the PR attach, 301–345 `newestFirst`/`listHomeRuns`/`listRuns`, 440–501 `git`/`landedChanges`, 543–577 `runDetail`) — run listing.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/runhome.ts` (whole file) — `RunHome`, `project~<id>` ids, `projectHome`, `resolveRunHome`, `homeAsWorkspace`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/pr.ts` (lines 80–92 `git`, 106–113 `specTitle`, 115–150 `suggest`/`remoteBranches`, 152–170 `prStatus`, 184–201 `preparePr`, 216–284 `runPrJob`, 311–338 `currentJob`/`startPr`) and `src/server/routes/pr.ts` — Create PR.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/specdone.ts` (whole file) — `moveSpecToDone` (fs + `git mv`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/workspaces.ts` (lines 59–70, 110–134 `runGit`, 170–265 the clone job: `gitAuthArgs`, `clone --progress`, `.git/info/exclude`) — the clone code `prepare` reuses.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/forges.ts` (lines 51–55 `gitAuthArgs`) — per-command auth header.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/workspaces.ts` (whole file) — `Workspace`, `resolveWorkspace`, `insideWorkspaces`, `listWorkspaces`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/projects.ts` (lines 1–80) — `projectDirOf`, `readProjectFile`, `PROJECTS_DIR`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/sandbox-run.ts` (lines 37–50) — `LOGIN_FILES`, `LOGIN_KEYS` (used by `loginFiles`).
