- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/terminals.test.ts` (lines 9–35) — PTY test skip rule (`process.platform === "win32"`) and helpers.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/bundle-imports.test.ts` — server code may import only the engine package's dependencies (no new npm deps).

## Patterns to follow

**Naming / file conventions:**
```
New folder apps/graph-manager/src/server/host/: types.ts (interfaces + HostError), local.ts (LocalWorkspaceHost),
contract.ts (the shared suite, NOT named *.test.ts so vitest does not run it directly), local.test.ts (runs the suite).
ESM imports with ".js" suffixes, as everywhere in src/server.
```

**The interface (copy exactly; the optional fields marked NEW are additions the spec's signature allows and later tasks rely on):**
```ts
// src/server/host/types.ts
import type { RunDetail, RunSummary } from "../runs.js";

export type ForgeKind = "github" | "gitlab";
export interface RepoRef { forge: ForgeKind; owner: string; name: string; baseUrl?: string }
/** Per-command forge auth: applied as `git -c http.extraHeader=…` (forges.ts gitAuthArgs), never written to .git/config. */
export interface GitAuth { forge: ForgeKind; token: string }
export type BranchChoice = { new: string } | { existing: string };
export type PrepareTarget = { repo: RepoRef } | { project: { id: string; repos: RepoRef[] } };

/** The subset of node-pty's IPty graph-manager uses; IPty is assignable to it. */
export interface PtyProcess {
  readonly pid: number;
  /** Foreground process name when known (node-pty `process`); remote PTYs may leave it undefined. */
  readonly process?: string;
  onData(cb: (data: string) => void): unknown;
  onExit(cb: (e: { exitCode: number }) => void): unknown;
  write(data: string): void;
  resize(cols: number, rows: number): void;
  kill(signal?: string): void;
}

/** Today's `Started` type of routes/runs.ts lines 87–100, moved here. */
export type EngineStart = { ok: true; stdout: string } | { ok: false; error: string; exitCode?: number; output: string };

export interface FileStat { kind: "file" | "dir" | "other"; size: number; mtimeMs: number; symlink: boolean }

export interface HostActivity { terminals: number; liveRuns: number; lastInputAt: string | null; lastOutputAt: string | null }

export interface WorkspaceHost {
  readonly kind: "local" | "remote";
  prepare(p: PrepareTarget & { branch: BranchChoice; cloneUrl?: string /* NEW */; auth?: GitAuth /* NEW */ }): Promise<{ workspaceId: string; branch: string }>;
  /** argv [] = the host's default shell. env is ADDED to the host's own terminal base env. cwd = the workspace. */
  spawnPty(p: { workspaceId: string; argv: string[]; env: Record<string, string>; cols: number; rows: number }): Promise<PtyProcess>;
  /** env is ADDED to the host's engine base env. resumeRunId (NEW): take over a foreign lock of that run, as resume does today. */
  startEngine(p: { workspaceId: string; args: string[]; env: Record<string, string>; timeoutMs: number; resumeRunId?: string }): Promise<EngineStart>;
  readFile(workspaceId: string, rel: string): Promise<string | undefined>;
  /** NEW: lstat-style info of a path inside the workspace; undefined when missing, absolute, or resolving outside it. */
  stat(workspaceId: string, rel: string): Promise<FileStat | undefined>;
  /** Files (not dirs, not symlinks) directly in `rel` matching `glob` (only `*` wildcards; default `*`), names sorted. */
  listFiles(workspaceId: string, rel: string, opts?: { glob?: string }): Promise<string[]>;
  listRuns(workspaceId: string): Promise<RunSummary[]>;
  runDetail(workspaceId: string, runId: string): Promise<RunDetail | undefined>;
  git(workspaceId: string, args: string[], opts?: { onStderr?: (chunk: string) => void; timeoutMs?: number } /* NEW */): Promise<{ exitCode: number; stdout: string; stderr: string }>;
  activity(): Promise<HostActivity>;
  changes(workspaceId: string): Promise<string[]>;
  save(p: { workspaceId: string; branch: string; message: string; auth?: GitAuth; filter?: (path: string) => boolean }): Promise<{ pushed: boolean; skipped: string[]; error?: string }>;
  discard(workspaceId: string): Promise<void>;
  loginFiles(op: "get" | "put", providers: string[], files?: Record<string, string>): Promise<Record<string, string>>;
  pushBranch(workspaceId: string, opts?: { auth?: GitAuth }): Promise<{ ok: boolean; error?: string }>;
}

/** A refused host operation; `status` is the HTTP status the route answers with `{ error: message }`. */
export class HostError extends Error {
  constructor(readonly status: number, message: string) { super(message); this.name = "HostError"; }
}
```

**Forge auth (answers "how is the token used without writing it to disk"):** every git command that talks to `origin` (`clone`, `fetch`, `push`) is run as `git ...gitAuthArgs(auth.forge, auth.token) <cmd>` — exactly what `routes/workspaces.ts` line 220 does for clone today (`[...gitAuthArgs(forge, token), "clone", "--progress", "--", repo.cloneUrl, dest]`). The token lives only on that one command line (a `-c http.extraHeader=Authorization: Basic …`), is never written to `.git/config`, and is scrubbed from every error message with `scrub(text, token)` (pr.ts line 94). Resolution order inside `LocalWorkspaceHost`: the per-call `auth` field wins; else the constructor option `forgeAuth?: (forge: ForgeKind) => Promise<GitAuth | undefined>`; else no auth (file:// remotes in tests need none). Callers (the sessions task) should pass `auth` per call, built from the user's own forge connection in their store (`us.get().forges.github.token` etc.), because the local host is shared between users and a remote host can only receive it per call.

**Routes get a host only through `ctx.hostFor`:**
```ts
// AppContext additions (app.ts)
localHost: LocalWorkspaceHost;
/** The ONLY way routes get a host. This task: always ctx.localHost. The sessions task makes it session-aware. */
hostFor(workspaceId: string, user: User): Promise<WorkspaceHost>;
```
No route may `new LocalWorkspaceHost` or import `host/local.ts` except `app.ts` (the type-only `instanceof`/`kind` checks are fine).

**Error handling:**
```ts
// app.ts setErrorHandler, BEFORE the generic statusCode branch (line 116): any status, including 5xx (a later task answers 503 through it)
if (err instanceof HostError) return reply.code(err.status).send({ error: err.message });
```
Routes keep their existing exact error strings (e.g. `tasksDir: ${body.tasksDir} is not a folder inside the workspace`, `spec not found`, `unknown workspace`).

**Git helper (mirror runs.ts lines 440–453 and pr.ts 89–92):**
```ts
const res = await execa("git", args, { cwd, env: { ...process.env, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT: "0" }, reject: false, stdin: "ignore", all: false, timeout });
return { exitCode: typeof res.exitCode === "number" ? res.exitCode : -1, stdout: String(res.stdout ?? ""), stderr: String(res.stderr ?? "") };
```
`host.git` does NOT trim stdout (callers that trimmed before trim themselves). With `onStderr`, attach `sub.stderr?.on("data", …)` like pr.ts line 234.

**Test pattern:** `routes/pr.test.ts` (fake forge + `appWithLogin`) for route tests; for the contract suite create the bare remote with plain git:
```ts
await execa("git", ["init", "--bare", "-q", "-b", "main", bare]);
// seed: clone into a temp dir, commit README.md, push main and a branch `feature` with one more commit
```

## Step-by-step tasks

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/host/types.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: exactly the block above. `RunSummary`/`RunDetail` are type-only imports from `../runs.js`.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/runs.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: extract the PR attach of `summarize` (lines 286–291) into `export function attachPr(summary: RunSummary, prs: PrIndex | undefined): RunSummary` and call it from `summarize` (behaviour unchanged). Export `newestFirst`. Add `export function attachPrs(runs: RunSummary[], prs: PrIndex | undefined): RunSummary[]`.
- **GOTCHA**: existing `runs.test.ts` must pass unchanged.

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/host/local.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: `export class LocalWorkspaceHost implements WorkspaceHost` with `readonly kind = "local"` and constructor options:
  ```ts
  { workspacesDir: string; graphExecutionBin: string; dataDir?: string /* view cache + reviewers */; binDir?: string; reviewersFile?: string;
    env?: NodeJS.ProcessEnv; shell?: string; platform?: NodeJS.Platform;
    /** Home folder whose agent login files loginFiles reads/writes; unset = no-op (local mode: the user's own home is used). */
    loginHome?: string;
    forgeAuth?: (forge: ForgeKind) => Promise<GitAuth | undefined> }
  ```
  - Path of a workspace id: `resolveWorkspace(workspacesDir, id)?.path`; for `project~<pid>` (`PROJECT_PREFIX` from runhome.ts, pid matching `/^[a-z0-9-]+$/`): `projectDirOf(workspacesDir, pid)` when `<dir>/.git` exists. Unknown → `throw new HostError(404, "unknown workspace")` (readFile/stat/runDetail return undefined instead, listRuns returns []).
  - `spawnPty`: `pty.spawn(file, args, { name: "xterm-256color", cols, rows, cwd: <workspace path>, env: { ...terminalEnv(opts.env ?? process.env, binDir, reviewersFile, platform), ...p.env } })` (argv `[]` → `[opts.shell ?? defaultShell(env)]`). Wrap the IPty so `write` sets `lastInputAt` and `onData` output sets `lastOutputAt`, and count live PTYs (decrement on exit) for `activity()`.
  - `startEngine`: move `engineCommand` + the execa call of `routes/runs.ts` lines 90–100 here. Base env (moved from `engineEnv` lines 77–85 and resume.ts 101–107): `{ ...process.env, GRAPH_EXECUTION_HANDOFF: "detached", SSH_CONNECTION: "1" }` minus `GM_PASSWORD` and `INTERNAL_ENV`, then `...p.env`. With `resumeRunId`: `const lock = await readLock(runDir).catch(() => undefined); if (lock && lock.host !== lockHost()) env.GRAPH_EXECUTION_TAKE_LOCK_FROM = lock.host;` (moved from resume.ts lines 102–105). cwd = workspace path. Keep `engineCommand`, `INTERNAL_ENV`, `START_TIMEOUT_MS`, `lastLines` exported from routes/runs.ts (re-export or import from local.ts; other modules import them).
  - `readFile`/`stat`/`listFiles`: reject absolute paths and `\0`; resolve inside the workspace with the realpath rule of `insideWorkspace` (routes/runs.ts lines 48–55); `stat` uses `lstat` for `symlink` and `stat` (following) for kind/size/mtimeMs. `listFiles` lists entries `isFile() && !isSymbolicLink()` whose name matches the glob (`*` → `[^/]*`, anchored), sorted by name.
  - `listRuns(id)`: `listHomeRuns(home, undefined, dataDir)`; `runDetail(id, runId)`: `runDetail(home, runId, dataDir)`. Build the `RunHome` from the path: workspace → `workspaceHome(ws)`; project → `{ kind: "project", id, path, project: { id: pid, name: (await readProjectFile(dir))?.name ?? pid, workspaces: [], createdAt: "" } }` (runs.ts `projectOf` only reads id and name). PRs are NOT attached here (routes call `attachPrs` with the user's `prs`).
  - `git`: the helper above with cwd = workspace path.
  - `activity()`: `{ terminals, liveRuns, lastInputAt, lastOutputAt }`; `liveRuns` = runs with `kind === "live"` over `listWorkspaces(workspacesDir)` plus every project folder under `<workspacesDir>/.projects/*` that has `.git`.
  - `changes(id)`: lines of `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- . ":(exclude).graph-execution"` (non-empty lines, untrimmed path part `line.slice(3)`).
  - `prepare`: only `{ repo }` here; `{ project }` throws `new HostError(501, "project sessions are not supported yet")` (the project-sessions task implements it). workspaceId = `[repo.forge, ...repo.owner.split("/"), repo.name].join("~")`, dest = `path.join(workspacesDir, repo.forge, ...repo.owner.split("/"), repo.name)`, checked with `insideWorkspaces`. Clone URL: `p.cloneUrl` else github `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>.git`, gitlab `${baseUrl ?? "https://gitlab.com"}/<owner>/<name>.git`. Missing clone → `git [...auth] clone -- <url> <dest>` then append `.graph-execution/\n` to `.git/info/exclude` (routes/workspaces.ts lines 243–244); on failure remove dest and throw `HostError(502, scrub("clone failed: " + lastLine(stderr), token))`. Existing → `git [...auth] fetch --prune origin` (failure → HostError 502 `fetch failed: …`). If the target branch differs from `git branch --show-current` and `changes()` is not empty → `throw new HostError(409, `${repo.owner}/${repo.name} has uncommitted changes. Close its session with Push or Discard first.`)`. `{ new: b }`: local `refs/heads/b` exists → HostError(409, `branch ${b} already exists`); else `git checkout -q -b b <origin default>` where the default is `git symbolic-ref --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` (fallback `origin/main`). `{ existing: b }`: local exists → `git checkout -q b` then `git merge -q --ff-only origin/b` (ignore its failure); else `origin/b` exists → `git checkout -q -b b --track origin/b`; else HostError(404, `branch ${b} not found`). Validate branch names with `git check-ref-format --branch` (pr.ts line 194 rule) → HostError(400, `invalid branch name: ${b}`). Returns `{ workspaceId, branch }`.
  - `save`: default skip rule exported as `export const isSecretPath = (p: string): boolean` matching the basename `.env`, `.env.*`, `*.pem`, `*.key`, `id_rsa*`. Paths = `changes()` paths (for renames `a -> b` use b); skipped = those where `isSecretPath(p) || (p.filter && !p.filter(path))`. Stage the rest with `git add -A -- <paths>` (git-ignored files never appear in status, so they are never staged). If something is staged, commit with message `p.message`, with the identity fallback of pr.ts lines 259–260 (`-c user.name=graph-manager -c user.email=graph-manager@localhost` when `user.email` is unset). Then `git [...auth] push origin HEAD:refs/heads/<branch>`; failure → `{ pushed: false, skipped, error: scrub(lastLine(stderr), token) }`. The `filter` option is how the sessions task plugs in its own rules (src/server/sessions/secrets.ts); it cannot cross the agent wire, so remote hosts apply `isSecretPath` only.
  - `discard`: `git reset -q --hard` then `git clean -fdq` (ignored files, including `.graph-execution/`, stay).
  - `pushBranch`: current branch from `git branch --show-current` (empty → `{ ok: false, error: "no branch checked out" }`), then `git [...auth] push -u origin HEAD:refs/heads/<branch>`.
  - `loginFiles`: no `loginHome` → return `{}` for both ops. With it: `get` reads every file of `LOGIN_FILES[p]` for each provider (a trailing `/` entry = all files under that folder, recursively) → `{ relPath: base64 }`; `put` writes each given file (base64 → bytes, mode 0o600, dirs 0o700) only when its relPath is one of those entries or under a folder entry, else `throw new HostError(400, `not a login file: ${rel}`)`; returns `{}`.
- **IMPORTS**: `node-pty`, `execa`, `graph-execution/api` (`readLock`, `lockHost`), `../terminals.js` (`terminalEnv`, `defaultShell`), `../runs.js`, `../runhome.js`, `../workspaces.js`, `../projects.js`, `../forges.js` (`gitAuthArgs`), `../pr.js` (`scrub`, `lastLine`), `../sandbox-run.js` (`LOGIN_FILES`).
- **GOTCHA**: no new npm dependencies (bundle-imports.test.ts). Avoid an import cycle with routes/runs.ts: move `engineCommand`/`INTERNAL_ENV`/`START_TIMEOUT_MS`/`lastLines` into a small `src/server/engine.ts` and re-export them from routes/runs.ts.

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/terminals.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: `Term.proc: PtyProcess` (from host/types). Add `async createOnHost(host: WorkspaceHost, p: CreateTerminal & { workspaceId: string }): Promise<TerminalInfo>` that builds the same Term but gets its process from `host.spawnPty({ workspaceId, argv: p.command ?? [], env: { ...this.opts.extraEnv?.(), ...p.env, GM_TERMINAL_ID: id }, cols, rows })`, writes `p.input`, and remembers `host` + `workspaceId` on the Term. Add `async restartAsync(id)`: host terms respawn through the host; others call the existing sync `restart`. Keep `create`/`restart` (sync, used by tests and cwd terminals) unchanged. `processOf` must accept `process` being undefined.
- **GOTCHA**: env must be identical to today for a local terminal: today `{ ...this.env, ...extraEnv(), ...termEnv, GM_TERMINAL_ID }` with `this.env = terminalEnv(...)`; the host prepends the same `terminalEnv(...)`, so build `LocalWorkspaceHost` in app.ts with the same `env`, `binDir`, `reviewersFile` as `TerminalManager`.

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: build `const localHost = new LocalWorkspaceHost({ workspacesDir, graphExecutionBin, dataDir, binDir: <same as terminals>, reviewersFile: reviewersFilePath(config.dataDir) })`; add `localHost` and `hostFor: async () => localHost` to `ctx`; add the `HostError` branch to the error handler.

### UPDATE routes
- `routes/terminals.ts`: with `workspaceId` (after the existing `resolveWorkspace` 404 check), `await terminals.createOnHost(await ctx.hostFor(ws.id, req.user), {...})` for both the plain and the agent branch; project/cwd terminals stay on `terminals.create`. Restart route → `await terminals.restartAsync(id)`.
- `routes/runs.ts`: `GET /api/runs` → for each `listWorkspaces(root)` id and each stored project (`project~<id>` whose `projectHome` resolves) `host.listRuns(id)`, flatten, `attachPrs(…, prs)`, sort `newestFirst`; with `?workspace=` the same for one id. `GET /api/runs/:ws/:runId` → `host.runDetail` then `attachPr(detail.summary, prs)`. Start: replace `insideWorkspace(ws, …)` existence checks with `host.stat(home.id, rel)` (undefined → the same 400 messages); non-sandboxed starts (workspace and project) call `host.startEngine({ workspaceId: home.id, args, env: { [RUN_ID_ENV]: runId, ...(existsSync(reviewersFile) ? { [REVIEWERS_ENV]: reviewersFile } : {}) }, timeoutMs: START_TIMEOUT_MS })`. Sandboxed branches (`ctx.sandboxes.start`, local Docker, KAN-88) stay exactly as they are.
- `routes/resume.ts`: non-sandboxed path reads `state.json`/`suite.json` with `host.readFile(home.id, `.graph-execution/${runId}/state.json`)` (parse with `stateSchema`/`suiteStateSchema`), liveness with `(await host.runDetail(home.id, runId))?.summary.live`, and starts with `host.startEngine({ workspaceId: home.id, args, env: {}, timeoutMs: START_TIMEOUT_MS, resumeRunId: runId })`, keeping the `SandboxError(400, tail, tail)` + `exitCode` on failure. Sandboxed paths unchanged.
- `routes/specs.ts`: `listSpecs(host, wsId)` and the file route via `host.listFiles(wsId, "docs/prd", { glob: "*.md" })` (case: also accept `.MD` — filter names with `/\.md$/i` and use glob `*`), `host.stat` (symlink → same 400 `INVALID_PATH`; size > MAX_SPEC_BYTES → 413), `host.readFile` (title from the first 64 KiB of the text). Same responses and ordering as today.
